(/* LONG COMMENT on sign conventions) N
(In most of the program, the KS phases and antiperiodic boundary) N
(conditions are absorbed into the link matrices.  This greatly simplfies) N
(multiplying by the fermion matrix.  However, it requires care in) N
(specifying the path coefficients.  Remember that each time you) N
(encircle a plaquette, you pick up a net minus sign from the KS phases.) N
(Thus, when you have more than one path to the same point, you generally) N
(have a relative minus sign for each plaquette in a surface bounded by) N
(this path and the basic path for that displacement.) N
() N
